#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started &mdash; the &appwizard;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "&appwizard;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kdevelop; software development work is organized in <emphasis>projects</"
"emphasis>. Such a project keeps everything together which belongs to a "
"complete programming task: source files, additional data files, any actually "
"needed management facilities as the make system as well as access to all "
"components and any additional tools needed to get the application up and "
"running."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Organizing all development work in projects allows you to easily switch "
"between the global tasks at hand. This is quite handy if you &eg; work on "
"several applications at the same time as is often the case. Tell &kdevelop; "
"to open the project you want to work at and you may proceed in the "
"environment just where you left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Projects"
msgstr ""

