#: applicationwizard.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>CVS</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>database</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:385 applicationwizard.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "version"
msgstr "version"

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>database</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In a second step the &appwizard; will lead you to the <guilabel>Version "
"Control System</guilabel> page where you can decide which version control "
"system you want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This discussion concentrates on the needs for project creation only. For "
"more information on &CVS; see the <link linkend=\"cvs\">Using &CVS;</link> "
"chapter below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "No Version Control System Wanted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Initially there is <quote>None</quote> selected in the <guilabel>Version "
"control system</guilabel> tab, and the page will be empty otherwise. If you "
"don't want to use a version control system, just click the <guibutton>Next "
"></guibutton> button and go on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &CVS;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Otherwise you must reselect the version control system you want to use from "
"the <guilabel>Version control system</guilabel> tab. We use <quote>&cvs;</"
"quote> for our example. If you select this, the &appwizard; will redisplay "
"the page, now showing a series of fields you must fill in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set new project up for CVS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A version control system such as &CVS; (which means <quote>Concurrent "
"Versions System</quote>) stores copies of selected project files in some "
"sort of a database. If you use &CVS; you can amongst others upload "
"(<quote>commit</quote>) those files or load them back into your project "
"directory (<quote>checkout</quote>, or <quote>update</quote>). The special "
"thing about this is that the files in the versioning database are stored in "
"a structured way which allows you to always revert to an earlier development "
"state if you need so. And &CVS; allows multiple designers to fairly easily "
"collaborate on a big project (such as &kdevelop;) without disturbing each "
"others work."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>root</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>root</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "local"
msgstr "locala"

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid "remote"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "local CVS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>:local:</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:446 applicationwizard.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>:local:</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "&CVS; Root"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&CVS; needs to <emphasis>manage</emphasis> the versioning database it keeps "
"from your project files. To accomplish this it keeps some special database "
"information in an own directory, called the <emphasis>&CVS; root</emphasis>. "
"The first step on setting up &CVS; for your new project thus is to tell "
"&kdevelop; where this root is located."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Local &CVS; root.</emphasis> There are two basic possibilities. "
"Either you want to use a <emphasis>local</emphasis> &CVS; database or you "
"use a database which is held on a <emphasis>remote server</emphasis>. If you "
"develop for your own, you may want use the &CVS; database as some sort of a "
"backup system on your own computer. Usually this is set up in your home "
"directory root and given the name <filename>cvsroot</filename>. This may "
"look as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><filename class=\"directory\">/home/devel/cvsroot</filename></"
"userinput> (where <filename>devel</filename> simply denotes the "
"<quote>developing</quote> user, just for example)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In fact, this is a short form. Exactly, the local &CVS; root should be "
"addressed using the <computeroutput>:local:</computeroutput> prefix. The "
"short form is only allowed in cases where the filename starts with a slash "
"(<computeroutput>/</computeroutput>). The full name for our example local "
"&CVS; root would exactly look like: <filename class=\"directory\">:local:/"
"home/devel/cvsroot</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the name of the &CVS; root directory your system has been set up for "
"in the <guilabel>CVS root</guilabel> field. In principle you can select any "
"name, even use multiple &CVS; databases, but it is advisable that you stick "
"to the &CVS; root once set up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Initialize a new &CVS; root.</emphasis> If there does not exist a "
"&CVS; root yet, &kdevelop; can command the &CVS; system to create one for "
"you in the given directory. Just check the <guilabel>Init root</guilabel> "
"checkbox below the <guilabel>CVS root</guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As said, &kdevelop; only <emphasis>commands</emphasis> the &CVS; system to "
"initialize a new &CVS; root. It does nothing by itself to this directory. "
"Fortunately &CVS; is clever enough to check whether the &CVS; root directory "
"already exists. Hence it does no harm if you should have inadvertently "
"checked <guilabel>Init root</guilabel> on an already existing &CVS; root "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Remote &CVS; root.</emphasis> There are occasions where the &CVS; "
"database is to be kept on a remote server, especially when several "
"developers work at the same project. Then you must enter the &CVS; root "
"&URL; of this server in the <guilabel>CVS root</guilabel> field. For "
"example, if you want access to the &kde; &CVS; server:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><filename class=\"directory\">:pserver:<replaceable>mylogin</"
"replaceable>@cvs.kde.org:/home/kde</filename></userinput> (where "
"<replaceable>mylogin</replaceable> denotes the login name set up in your "
"&kde; &CVS; account)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "remote CVS"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>:pserver:</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>:ext:</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>:pserver:</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>:ext:</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote &CVS; Server Types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Basically there are two widely used remote &CVS; server types, the "
"<emphasis>pserver</emphasis> which uses a password-secured non-encrypted "
"protocol, and the <emphasis>ext</emphasis> server which uses an rsh or ssh "
"encrypted data transfer. They are distinguished by the &URL; prefix they use:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: applicationwizard.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>:pserver:</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid "for the <quote>password protected server</quote> non-encrypted type, and"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: applicationwizard.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>:ext:</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "for an rsh or ssh encrypted server type. For example"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: applicationwizard.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
":ext:<replaceable>mylogin</replaceable>@cvs.cervisia.sourceforge.net:/"
"cvsroot/cervisia"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"accesses the &CVS; root of the widely used <application>Cervisia</"
"application> &CVS; management tool on the SourceForge server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use an rsh or ssh encrypted server for &CVS; access you must "
"tell &kdevelop; the encryption protocol to be used. Just enter "
"<userinput>rsh</userinput> or <userinput>ssh</userinput> in the "
"<guilabel>CVS_RSH</guilabel> field of the <guilabel>Create New Project</"
"guilabel> <guilabel>Version Control System</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a caveat if you use an encrypted server for &CVS; from within "
"&kdevelop;. See the <link linkend=\"cvs\">Using &CVS;</link> chapter for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>repository</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>repository</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &CVS; Repository"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So far you have told &kdevelop; where the &CVS; root resides which manages "
"the versioning database and how to access it. Now you need to tell "
"&kdevelop; under which name you want &CVS; save your project files in that "
"database. Such a place your project files will be held in &CVS; is called a "
"<emphasis>repository</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In principle you can use any name for the &CVS; repository of your project "
"files as long as it adheres to the specifications of naming a file. Yet, "
"most developers simply use the name of the application itself. &CVS; will "
"build a directory with this name in the &CVS; root, hence it is more easily "
"found if you keep the application name for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just enter the repository name you want to use in the <guilabel>CVS "
"repository</guilabel> field of the <guilabel>Create New Project</guilabel> "
"<guilabel>Version Control System</guilabel> page. In our example this is: "
"<userinput>MyApp</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Take care not to use a repository which already exists!</emphasis> "
"The &CVS; system does not warn about duplicate files but will shovel "
"everything in which does not produce a formal conflict. You will mess up "
"everything!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Remaining Fields"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is not much work left to do. &appwizard; has already set up the "
"remaining fields for you. In detail:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Vendor</guilabel> field is used for compatibility reasons "
"only. You can stick to the <quote>vendor</quote> default the &appwizard; "
"puts in here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Message</guilabel> field allows you to comment the initial "
"&CVS; contents. Use any text you like or just stick to the <quote>new "
"project</quote> default the &appwizard; did put in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Release tag</guilabel> holds the name which tags the initial "
"state of your project. Such a <emphasis>tag</emphasis> names a certain point "
"within the &CVS; repository by which you can later access this state of your "
"development. (See more in the <link linkend=\"cvs\">Using &CVS;</link> "
"chapter.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &appwizard; has put a default <quote>start</quote> tag in here which is "
"a worthy proposal. Just stick to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When any information of all these is wrong &kdevelop; usually will not know "
"about until project construction time. It is the &CVS; system which will "
"figure out those errors when it tries to build the repository. Hence you "
"must keep an eye to the <guilabel>Messages</guilabel> window of &kdevelop; "
"when the project is created in the final setup step. If anything was in "
"error with &CVS; you will in most cases see an error message like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"* cd '/home/devel/test' &amp;&amp; cvs -d '/home/devel/mycvsroot' \\\n"
"  import -m 'new project' '' 'vendor' 'start' &amp;&amp;\\\n"
"  sh /opt/kde3/share/apps/kdevcvs/buildcvs.sh . '' \\\n"
"  '/home/devel/mycvsroot'\n"
"* cvs [import aborted]: /home/devel/mycvsroot/CVSROOT: No such file or\n"
"  directory\n"
"* *** Exited with status: 1 ***\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this happens you will have to either manually set up &CVS; (&kdevelop; "
"should have successfully initialized your project files at this time) or "
"delete the project directory and start over again with <guimenuitem>New "
"Project</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>Project</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered all &CVS; related information, click the "
"<guibutton>Next &gt;</guibutton> to go on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to correct an error on the previous <guilabel>Create New "
"Project</guilabel> page, just press the <guibutton>&lt; Back</guibutton> "
"button. The &appwizard; will remember your settings on the current page, so "
"you can easily proceed when you come back."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supply Header/Source Templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next step brings you to a series of pages where you can set up common "
"information you want to include in your source and header files, if the task "
"at hand allows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Both header and source templates are provided for C and C++ applications, "
"each on its own page. For other languages there may be source templates "
"only. And in some cases you will even find this template page empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the page is used, &appwizard; will fill in some common header comment "
"which for a C++ based application might look like:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput><literal>\n"
"/"
"***************************************************************************\n"
" *   Copyright (C) 2003 by Your Name                                       "
"*\n"
" *   you@you.com                                                           "
"*\n"
" *                                                                         "
"*\n"
" *   This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify  "
"*\n"
" *   it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by  "
"*\n"
" *   the Free Software Foundation; either version 2 of the License, or     "
"*\n"
" *   (at your option) any later version.                                   "
"*\n"
" *                                                                         "
"*\n"
" *   This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,       "
"*\n"
" *   but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of        "
"*\n"
" *   MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the         "
"*\n"
" *   GNU General Public License for more details.                          "
"*\n"
" *                                                                         "
"*\n"
" *   You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License     "
"*\n"
" *   along with this program; if not, write to the                         "
"*\n"
" *   Free Software Foundation, Inc.,                                       "
"*\n"
" *   51 Franklin Street, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA  02110-1301, "
"USA.             *\n"
" ***************************************************************************/\n"
"</literal></computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other templates will provide similar information in a format according to "
"the definitions of the programming language you want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you might have noticed, the applications manager did readily fill in some "
"information you provided on the first <guilabel>General</guilabel> page of "
"the <guilabel>Create New Project</guilabel> dialog, namely the contents of "
"the <guilabel>Author</guilabel> and <guilabel>Email</guilabel> fields. Also "
"proper license information will have been inserted according to your "
"selection in the <guilabel>License</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Edit the Templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:626 applicationwizard.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid "edit"
msgstr "edicion"

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The templates you set up in the <guilabel>Create New Project</guilabel> "
"dialog will later be processed whenever you command &kdevelop; to set up a "
"new source and/or header file. The information you provided here will be "
"included at top as a documentation header, before the code parts begin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are not restricted to plain text however. &kdevelop; knows of several "
"variables which allow you to include actual information in the file. The "
"&appwizard; did in fact use some such variables to insert the "
"<guilabel>Author</guilabel>, <guilabel>Email</guilabel>, and "
"<guilabel>License</guilabel> informations into the initial template text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: applicationwizard.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include &doxygen; File Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If, for example, you want the &doxygen;-built &API; documentation to display "
"some further information about the file's contents in its filenames list, "
"you may include the following lines in the source file template:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"/**\n"
" * \\file $MODULE$.cpp\n"
" * \\brief (put some short descripion here).\n"
" **/\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whenever you create a new source file, &kdevelop; will replace the <varname>"
"$MODULE$</varname> variable by the name body of the newly created file. For "
"example, if you created a new C++ class named <classname>ASimpleTest</"
"classname> you will see the following lines in the <filename>asimpletest."
"cpp</filename> file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"/**\n"
" * \\file asimpletest.cpp\n"
" * \\brief (put some short descripion here).\n"
" **/\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will still have to provide the short description after the <quote>"
"\\brief</quote> keyword, but part of the job is automatically done for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: applicationwizard.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "The License Text File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As another example you could include an explicit hint to the license text "
"you want to use into the template. Use the <varname>$LICENSEFILE$</varname> "
"variable for this and add for example this line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:664
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"//   See $LICENSEFILE$ for the full license text.\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &appwizard; will replace the <varname>$LICENSEFILE$</varname> with the "
"name of the file where the full license text is to be found, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"//   See COPYING for the full license text.\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid "for the <acronym>GPL</acronym> license, or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: applicationwizard.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>\n"
"//   See LICENSE.BSD for the full license text.\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if you decided to put your application under the <acronym>BSD</acronym> "
"license."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Thee are of course more variables &kdevelop; knows of. See the <link linkend="
"\"newfiles-edittemplates\">Editing the templates</link> section in the <link "
"linkend=\"editing\">Editing tools</link> chapter for what is possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The templates you define here will come in effect only after the &appwizard; "
"has created the new project. You will find this information on top of the "
"files you created yourself in the development process. When creating the "
"initial files the &appwizard; will use some predefined standard templates. "
"You will have to manually adapt those initial files to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: applicationwizard.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Build the Initial Project Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: tertiary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid "build"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: applicationwizard.docbook:699
#, no-c-format
msgid "initial build"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Almost everything is done now. On the last templates page the "
"<guibutton>Next &gt;</guibutton> button will have changed to read "
"<guibutton>Finish</guibutton> now."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Think twice before you click on it!</emphasis> You still have the "
"option to revise everything by repeatedly using the <guibutton>&lt; Back</"
"guibutton> button. As the &appwizard; remembers all information you did "
"input so far, it may be advisable for you to take the time and look back "
"once again. In case you use local &CVS;, do not forget to double-check the "
"<emphasis>&CVS; repository</emphasis> name (there should be no subdirectory "
"with that name in the &CVS; root directory already&mdash;if it does, try "
"another repository name)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If ever you don't want the new project be built, abort the <guilabel>Create "
"New Project</guilabel> dialog by the <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> button. "
"Otherwise click <guibutton>Finish</guibutton> and watch in the "
"<guilabel>Messages</guilabel> window how the &appwizard; initiates the "
"project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to use a versioning system (&CVS;) there will be two runs "
"actually. &appwizard; will first build the project directories and files and "
"then call up the &CVS; program which restarts the <guilabel>Messages</"
"guilabel> window with its own contents. If any error occurs in either of "
"these runs, the process will stop showing you an according error message in "
"the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In many cases when your new project has been set up this way, &kdevelop; "
"will automatically load the source file(s) of one or more basically "
"important modules so you can readily start work. (Which source modules will "
"be displayed&mdash;if any at all&mdash;however depends on the template "
"initially selected in the &appwizard;.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not forget to initially check what the &appwizard; has provided. For "
"example you may want to change the initial heading informations according to "
"your own templates. Usually you will find these in a <filename class="
"\"directory\">templates</filename> subdirectory in your project directory. "
"Some simple copy operations will mostly suffice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: applicationwizard.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then it is advisable that you <emphasis>compile the initial project</"
"emphasis> before you attempt to change any code. In most cases this initial "
"compilation should be possible. Thus you can make up whether the project "
"really was set up according to your needs. If it was not, simply remove the "
"project directory (in your local &CVS; root as well if you use one) and "
"start over again."
msgstr ""

